{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a temporary 10p fuel duty cut when petrol prices exceed \u00a31.65 a litre",
        "additional_details": "We want the Government to introduce temporary fuel-duty relief when fuel prices are exceptionally high.\r\n\r\nWhen the average UK petrol price exceeds \u00a31.65 per litre, fuel duty should be reduced by 10p per litre. The reduction should remain until average prices stay below \u00a31.65 per litre for four consecutive weeks.\r\n\r\nThis would give motorists targeted support without permanently reducing fuel-duty revenue.",
        "background": "Introduce a temporary 10p-per-litre reduction in fuel duty whenever the average UK petrol price exceeds \u00a31.65 per litre, with the full duty rate restored once prices fall below this level for a sustained period.",
